apeiron.machine.quantum_enhancement_module.desc=§bQuantum Force Transformer: guaranteed outputs and pattern catalysts§r\n§7Placement: replaces a bottom hatch or machine casing position§r\n§7Item and fluid output chances are fixed at 100%§r\n§7Set a catalyst programming circuit in the Infinite Pattern Input Assembly§r\n§7Uses the active pattern; no Bulk Catalyst Housing or physical catalyst needed§r\n§7Patterns keep materials and catalysts separate; mirrors are supported§r\n§7Infinite Energy Hatch: adjustable parallel and voltage§r\n§7Ultimate Infinite Energy Hatch: adjustable parallel and time§r\n§eSettings: use the machine controller power panel§r\n§7Keeps recipe tiers and fluid mode; no extra focusing plasma needed§r\n§6Note: ingredients, energy and output space are still required§r
apeiron.machine.quantum_enhancement_module.outputs=Item and fluid output chance: 100%
apeiron.machine.quantum_enhancement_module.catalyst=Catalyst: the active isolated pattern's programming circuit
apeiron.machine.quantum_enhancement_module.power=Configure parallel, voltage or time in the controller's power panel
apeiron.machine.eye_of_harmony_enhancement_module.duration=Runtime (ticks)
apeiron.machine.eye_of_harmony_enhancement_module.success_chance=Success chance (0 to 1)
apeiron.machine.eye_of_harmony_enhancement_module.desc=§bAdjusts Eye of Harmony runtime and success chance§r\n§7Placement: replaces one input hatch position§r\n§eSettings: right-click the module§r\n§7Default time: 128 ticks (6.4 seconds); minimum: 1 tick§r\n§7Default success chance: 0.5 (50%); range: 0 to 1§r\n§7Successful runs = parallel count × success chance§r\n§7Any fractional run gets a chance to succeed§r\n§7Removes the Astral Array limit; consecutive recipes can join within 1 tick§r\n§7Supports Infinite Storage Input Hatches, Buses and Assemblies§r\n§6Note: retains the Eye of Harmony total energy rules§r
gt.blockmachines.apeiron.infinite_pattern_input.name=Infinite Pattern Input Assembly
gt.blockmachines.apeiron.infinite_pattern_input_mirror.name=Infinite Pattern Input Assembly Mirror
apeiron.machine.infinite_pattern_input.desc=§bSupplies multiblocks from ME autocrafting patterns§r\n§7360 pattern slots; scroll to view all patterns§r\n§724 separate recipe buffers keep ingredients apart§r\n§7Each buffer holds 32 item and 32 fluid types§r\n§7Supports huge quantities; multipliers are saved separately§r\n§eControls: right-side button switches patterns / multipliers§r\n§eControls: bottom-right button opens buffer contents§r\n§eControls: + sets shared catalysts; middle-click a pattern for its own§r\n§7Catalyst slots are for ingredients the recipe does not consume§r\n§7Supports Programmable Hatches programming circuits§r\n§eControls: wire cutter changes ME connection sides§r
apeiron.machine.infinite_pattern_mirror.desc=§bShares one pattern input assembly across machines§r\n§7Uses the source patterns and stock; no extra AE channel§r\n§eControls: left-click source with a data stick, then right-click mirror§r\n§eControls: right-click the mirror to access the source§r\n§7Keeps its link when moved to a new position§r\n§6Note: the source chunk must stay loaded§r
