apeiron.machine.me_beamline_output_hatch.desc=§bConverts beamline outputs into particle items for ME storage§r\n§7Replaces ordinary or advanced beamline output hatches§r\n§7One ME connection with an unlimited particle buffer§r\n§7Keeps particles while disconnected; sends them after reconnecting§r\n§7Optional item cell provides partition filtering and cache mode§r\n§7Rejected particles wait until filtering allows them§r\n§eWire cutter changes ME sides; screwdriver toggles cache mode§r
apeiron.machine.me_beamline_output_hatch.pending=Particles waiting for output: %s
apeiron.machine.infinite_energy.desc=§bWireless GT power with configurable large parallel counts§r\n§eSettings: set parallel and voltage in the machine power panel§r\n§7Default parallel limit: 2,147,483,647§r\n§7Set parallel to 0 for no fixed limit§r\n§7Parallel and voltage accept scientific notation, e.g. 1E10§r\n§7Follows the machine's own overclock rules§r\n§6Note: higher voltage may cause lossy overclocking§r\n§7Inputs, wireless balance and output space still limit parallel§r\n§7Pauses on insufficient energy; resumes when power is available§r
apeiron.machine.ultimate_energy.desc=§bWireless GT power with adjustable parallel and completion time§r\n§eSettings: use the machine power panel§r\n§7Default parallel limit: 2,147,483,647; 0 removes the limit§r\n§7Parallel accepts scientific notation, e.g. 1E20§r\n§7Default time: 128 ticks (6.4 seconds at normal tick rate)§r\n§7Minimum: 1 tick; shorter time does not raise total energy use§r\n§7Charges the recipe base total energy to the wireless network§r\n§6Note: inputs, energy and output space still limit parallel§r
